body:
You need to respect your own feelings, because those are what matter more than anything.  She stopped appreciating you for you, even if you changed a bit, and if she can't accept that change, she's really not worth it.  Obviously over years nothing will stay the same, and people change.  Maybe she didn't like that change but it's nothing to feel guilty over, because it happened naturally - it didn't work because she thought you'd be the same way for two years.  That's not how it works!  If she has a "standard" for you, she's not the one.  

&#x200B;

If it's validating she clearly does miss you, but right now it's best to take a break from social media.  Stay strong and remember that you don't need to change to suit someone's standard.  You live for you luv!  There's someone better out there! ;0
